From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] lib: string: memmove copies backward a word at a time

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

Without an architecture memmove (arm64 has none unless USE_ARCH_MEMCPY is
set), an overlapping move to a higher address copied one byte at a time.
That is the move libfdt makes for every property it adds or grows:
everything after the insertion point goes up by the property's size. On a
Cortex-A53 at 816 MHz, adding thirty properties to a 110 KB device tree in
ft_board_setup took 22 ms, almost all of it in this loop.

When the source and destination ends are aligned alike, the backward copy
now goes a long at a time, or 32 bits at a time when they share only 4-byte
alignment (libfdt moves by multiples of four). Leading and trailing bytes
are copied as before. Each word is loaded before it is stored, and every
store lands above the bytes still to be read, so any overlap is safe. The
forward case is unchanged (memcpy).

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 lib/string.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/string.c b/lib/string.c
index dbf2ce34..042ed5e1 100644
--- a/lib/string.c
+++ b/lib/string.c
@@ -598,9 +598,33 @@ __rcode __used void *memmove(void *dest, const void *src, size_t count)
 	} else {
 		tmp = (char *) dest + count;
 		s = (char *) src + count;
+		/*
+		 * Backward, a word at a time where both ends align alike: growing a flattened
+		 * device tree moves everything after the insertion up by a multiple of four
+		 * bytes (thirty properties added to a 110 KB tree took 22 ms one byte at a
+		 * time on a 816 MHz Cortex-A53). Each word is read before it is written and
+		 * the writes stay above what is left to read, so any overlap is safe.
+		 */
+		if (!(((ulong)tmp ^ (ulong)s) & (sizeof(long) - 1))) {
+			for (; count && ((ulong)tmp & (sizeof(long) - 1)); count--)
+				*--tmp = *--s;
+			for (; count >= sizeof(long); count -= sizeof(long)) {
+				tmp -= sizeof(long);
+				s -= sizeof(long);
+				*(unsigned long *)tmp = *(unsigned long *)s;
+			}
+		} else if (!(((ulong)tmp ^ (ulong)s) & 3)) {
+			for (; count && ((ulong)tmp & 3); count--)
+				*--tmp = *--s;
+			for (; count >= 4; count -= 4) {
+				tmp -= 4;
+				s -= 4;
+				*(u32 *)tmp = *(u32 *)s;
+			}
+		}
 		while (count--)
 			*--tmp = *--s;
-		}
+	}
 
 	return dest;
 }
